-- title:
--   Non-archimedean Łojasiewicz bound for a function on X₀(N)
-- statement:
--   Let $N\ge 1$ and let $\bar F =$ `modularFunctionFieldBar N` be the subfield of the Laurent series field over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ generated over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ by the images of the modular function field $\mathbb Q$-generated by the divisor expansions of level $N$. Let $s : \mathrm{Fin}\,r \to \bar F$ satisfy `IsEmbBasis N s`, i.e. $s$ is linearly independent over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ and spans the Riemann–Roch space of the divisor `embDivisor N` $=$ `embDegree N` times the cusp at infinity; let $h \in \bar F$ be non-zero and let $p$ be a prime. The assertion is that there exist real constants $C \ge 0$ and $M > 0$ such that for every non-archimedean absolute value $\mu$ on $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ with $\mu(p) < 1$, every place $R$ of $\bar F$ over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ (a valuation subring containing $\overline{\mathbb Q}$, proper, and a principal ideal ring) and every real $L \ge 0$, if every place $Q$ with $Q.\mathrm{ord}\,h > 0$ (a zero of $h$) satisfies $\mathrm{prox}_\mu(\mathrm{evalVec}\,s\,R, \mathrm{evalVec}\,s\,Q) \le L$, then $$-C\bigl(-\log \mu(p)\bigr) - ML \;\le\; \min\bigl(0, \log \mu(R.\mathrm{evalAt}\,h)\bigr).$$ Here $\mathrm{evalVec}\,s\,v$ is the vector of residues of $s_i \cdot s_{j(v)}^{-1}$ at $v$, with $j(v)$ an index minimising the order $v.\mathrm{ord}(s_i)$; $R.\mathrm{evalAt}\,h$ is the residue of $h$ at $R$, taken to be $0$ when $h$ lies outside the valuation subring of $R$; and $\mathrm{prox}_\mu(x,y) = \log \sup_i \mu(x_i) + \log \sup_i \mu(y_i) - \log \sup_{k,l} \mu(x_k y_l - x_l y_k)$ is the chordal proximity of the two coordinate rows. The constants $C$ and $M$ depend only on $N$, $s$, $h$ and $p$, not on $\mu$, $R$ or $L$.
--
--   This is a non-archimedean Łojasiewicz-type inequality for a fixed element of the function field of $X_0(N)$, uniform in the absolute value: the residue $h(R)$ can be $\mu$-adically small only when $R$ is chordally close to some zero of $h$, the admissible closeness being controlled linearly in $L$ and in $-\log\mu(p)$. It is used in the height-theoretic analysis of charts on $X_0(N)$, being cited by [`ModularCurve.JZero.exists_chart_of_isPivot`](thm.html#ModularCurve.JZero.exists_chart_of_isPivot).
-- source:
